{"id":"af02d3b2fe1e4155bc9f0d69067611da","object":"chat.completion","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"v\":1,\"round\":42,\"nonce\":\"5eed5eed5eed5eed\",\"action\":\"bet\",\"market\":\"PENGU\",\"side\":\"long\",\"margin_e6\":\"11000000\",\"leverage\":1}","reasoning_content":"Let me think through this carefully.\n\nI'm the Intern, rank INTERN, an AI trader. I need to decide this round's bet among DOGE, SHIB, PEPE, PENGU, all long-only, max leverage 1, max margin $20M (e6 units), min notional $11M (e6 units). I have 1 bet left. Playbook: none.\n\nThe market data shows:\n- DOGE: 0.069137 USD, 24h +3.31%\n- SHIB: 0.004489 USD per 1,000 SHIB, 24h +3.65%\n- PEPE: 0.005005 USD per 1,000 PEPE, 24h -4.32%\n- PENGU: 0.006394 USD, 24h +5.27%\n\nAll prices dropped several digits — these are micro-cap meme coins at 2026 prices apparently. Everything is down massively from historical norms (DOGE at $0.069, SHIB at $0.0000045 per token which they quote per 1,000, PEPE per 1,000 at 0.005005, PENGU at 0.006394).\n\nI have to make a decision: bet or skip. With only momentum data (24h changes), the simplest heuristic is momentum-following: pick the strongest 24h mover. PENGU is +5.27%, the highest. DOGE +3.31%, SHIB +3.65%, PEPE -4.32% (negative).\n\nBut wait — as a cautious \"Intern\" rank, and given no playbook, maybe skip? The rules say answer with exactly one line of JSON, either skip or bet. The environment expects me to decide.\n\nGiven the data, the reasonable choice: long the strongest performer, PENGU, with a modest margin. Notional must be at least $11M e6, i.e., margin × leverage ≥ 11,000,000. With leverage 1, margin must be ≥ 11,000,000 (i.e., $11). Max margin is 20,000,000 ($20).\n\nWait, let me reconsider units: \"Amounts are US dollars times 1,000,000, so 10000000 is $10.\" So 11,000,000 e6 = $11. Max margin 20,000,000 = $20. So bets are between $11 and $20 notional effectively at 1x leverage. Tiny amounts. Fine.\n\nSo the bet: PENGU, long